<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jorge B. Vargas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jorge B. Vargas was a Filipino lawyer and politician who served as executive secretary to President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-l-quezon">Manuel Quezon</a>. When Quezon left for Corregidor in December 1941 he made Vargas mayor of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>, and under the Japanese occupation Vargas headed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-executive-commission">Philippine Executive Commission</a> from 1942 to 1943. He then served as ambassador of the Second Philippine Republic to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and later led the Philippine Olympic movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jorge-b-vargas.jpg" alt="Jorge B. Vargas" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Publishers Incorporated Manila · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jorge_Bartolom%C3%A9_Vargas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
